<body>

<main class="page">

    <header class="header">

        <div>

            <a
                href="https://ciga-website.ciga-hq.workers.dev/home"
                class="header-title"
            >
                CIGA SYSTEMS
            </a>

            <div class="header-subtitle">
                USER DOCUMENTATION // HELP
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="header-right">

            APPLICATION HELP<br>
            USER GUIDE

        </div>

    </header>


    <section class="intro">

        <div class="intro-label">
            CIGA APPLICATION
        </div>

        <h1 class="intro-title">
            HELP &amp; DOCUMENTATION
        </h1>

        <p class="intro-text">
            This page explains how to configure the main parts of CIGA:
            avatars, objects, interactions, settings, StreamElements,
            VMC, events, performance and the final viewport.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- =================================================
         01 AVATAR
    ================================================== -->

    <section class="help-section">

        <div class="section-header">

            <span class="section-number">
                01
            </span>

            <h2 class="section-title">
                IMPORTING AN AVATAR
            </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="section-content">

            <p>
                Adding an avatar is designed to be as automatic as possible.
                You do not normally need to manually configure the bones for
                a compatible VRM avatar.
            </p>

            <div class="steps">

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        01
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Click <strong>IMPORT CHARACTER</strong> and select
                        your <strong>.VRM</strong> avatar file.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        02
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Click <strong>LOAD AVATAR</strong>.
                        CIGA loads the avatar into the application.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        03
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Click <strong>MAP AVATAR</strong>.
                        CIGA automatically looks for the required bones and
                        creates the mapping.
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    AUTO MAPPING
                </div>

                CIGA includes automatic avatar bone mapping. For compatible
                avatars, the system can identify the expected bones and
                create the required hit point mapping for you.

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    SAVED MAPPING
                </div>

                Once the avatar has been mapped, its mapping is saved.
                You normally do not need to map the same avatar again.

            </div>

            <p style="margin-top: 20px;">

                You can also enable
                <span class="command">
                    LOAD CHARACTER ON LAUNCH
                </span>

                so the selected avatar is loaded automatically when CIGA
                starts.

            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =================================================
         02 OBJECTS
    ================================================== -->

    <section class="help-section">

        <div class="section-header">

            <span class="section-number">
                02
            </span>

            <h2 class="section-title">
                IMPORTING OBJECTS
            </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="section-content">

            <p>
                CIGA supports importing 3D objects in
                <strong>GLB</strong> and <strong>GLTF</strong> format.
                Imported objects can then be configured and used as
                interaction objects.
            </p>

            <div class="feature-grid">

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        OPTIMIZER
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        The optimizer creates a CIGA cache for the object.
                        It can remove unnecessary nodes, prepare materials
                        and reduce oversized textures where appropriate.
                        The original model is not modified.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        AUTO SCALE
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        Auto Scale is mainly intended for objects that are
                        extremely large compared with the character.
                        CIGA calculates the model bounds and applies a
                        smaller starting scale so the object can be used
                        at a more reasonable size.
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    AUTO SCALE IS NOT A UNIVERSAL NORMALIZER
                </div>

                Auto Scale does not try to resize every imported object.
                Its main purpose is to prevent unusually large models from
                entering CIGA at an impractical size. Smaller or normally
                sized models may keep a scale much closer to their original
                dimensions.

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    IMPORTANT
                </div>

                CIGA does its best to calculate a useful result, but every
                3D model is different. The importer cannot understand every
                modelling decision automatically, so always check the
                preview and adjust the object when necessary.
            </div>

            <div class="steps">

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        01
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Import the <strong>GLB</strong> or
                        <strong>GLTF</strong> object.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        02
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Enable <strong>OPTIMIZER</strong> when you want CIGA
                        to create an optimized runtime cache.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        03
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Enable <strong>AUTO SCALE</strong> when the object is
                        unusually large and needs a more practical starting
                        size.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        04
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Check the <strong>3D PREVIEW</strong> and manually
                        adjust the scale when required.
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =================================================
         03 INTERACTION
    ================================================== -->

    <section class="help-section">

        <div class="section-header">

            <span class="section-number">
                03
            </span>

            <h2 class="section-title">
                INTERACTION TESTING
            </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="section-content">

            <p>
                The Interaction page is a testing environment. It lets you
                preview how the avatar reacts when an object reaches one of
                the configured hit points.
            </p>

            <div class="steps">

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        01
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Choose the object you want to test.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        02
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Choose the target hit point, such as the
                        <strong>HEAD</strong>, <strong>CHEST</strong>,
                        <strong>SHOULDER</strong>, <strong>ARM</strong>
                        or <strong>LEG</strong>.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        03
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Choose the object spawn position and configure the
                        interaction values.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        04
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Launch the test object and watch the avatar response.
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    TEST PAGE
                </div>

                The Interaction page is mainly intended for testing and
                experimentation. It is useful for finding settings that feel
                correct before using the event system or final viewport.

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =================================================
         04 SETTINGS
    ================================================== -->

    <section class="help-section">

        <div class="section-header">

            <span class="section-number">
                04
            </span>

            <h2 class="section-title">
                SETTINGS
            </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="section-content">

            <p>
                The Settings page contains the configuration used by CIGA
                during normal operation.
            </p>

            <div class="feature-grid">

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        OBJECT SETTINGS
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        Configure values such as object speed, lifetime,
                        bounce behaviour and other object-related parameters.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        IMPACT SETTINGS
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        Configure how strongly the avatar reacts when an
                        object reaches a hit point.
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    TESTING VS FINAL SETTINGS
                </div>

                Use the Interaction page to experiment with behaviour.
                Use the Settings page when you want to define the values
                that CIGA should use during normal operation.

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =================================================
         05 STREAM ELEMENTS / VMC
    ================================================== -->

    <section class="help-section">

        <div class="section-header">

            <span class="section-number">
                05
            </span>

            <h2 class="section-title">
                SE / VMC
            </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="section-content">

            <p>
                CIGA can connect to external services used for stream
                integration and avatar output.
            </p>

            <div class="feature-grid">

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        STREAM ELEMENTS
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        StreamElements can be connected to CIGA for
                        stream-related events and integrations.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        VMC
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        VMC is used to send avatar movement and bone data
                        from CIGA to compatible external applications.
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    VMC PORT
                </div>

                CIGA currently sends its VMC output through
                <span class="command">
                    UDP 127.0.0.1:39539
                </span>

                on the local computer. This address is intended for
                communication with software running on the same machine.

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    CONNECTION
                </div>

                Make sure the external application is running and configured
                to receive the relevant CIGA output before testing the
                connection.

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =================================================
         06 EVENTS
    ================================================== -->

    <section class="help-section">

        <div class="section-header">

            <span class="section-number">
                06
            </span>

            <h2 class="section-title">
                EVENTS
            </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="section-content">

            <p>
                Events allow CIGA to perform configured actions when a
                supported trigger occurs.
            </p>

            <div class="steps">

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        01
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Open the <strong>EVENTS</strong> section.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        02
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Create or select the event you want to configure.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        03
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Configure the trigger and the action that should
                        happen when that trigger occurs.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        04
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Save the event configuration and test it with the
                        connected integration.
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    EVENTS ARE CONFIGURABLE
                </div>

                The exact behaviour depends on the trigger and actions
                selected in the event configuration.

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =================================================
         07 PERFORMANCE
    ================================================== -->

    <section class="help-section">

        <div class="section-header">

            <span class="section-number">
                07
            </span>

            <h2 class="section-title">
                OBJECTS &amp; PERFORMANCE
            </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="section-content">

            <p>
                CIGA is designed so that having many objects in the library
                does not automatically mean that all of them are being
                rendered at the same time.
            </p>

            <div class="feature-grid">

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        LIBRARY VS ACTIVE OBJECTS
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        You can keep a large number of objects in your CIGA
                        library. Objects stored in the library are not all
                        rendered continuously. The heavier part of the work
                        happens when resources are imported, prepared,
                        prewarmed or actively displayed.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        PROJECTILES
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        Interaction objects are created from already prepared
                        resources where possible. This avoids repeatedly
                        importing the same model during a burst.
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="workflow">

                <div class="workflow-item">

                    <div class="workflow-title">
                        CPU
                    </div>

                    <div class="workflow-text">
                        Handles tasks such as importing, preparing resources,
                        application logic, events and other runtime work.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="workflow-item">

                    <div class="workflow-title">
                        GPU
                    </div>

                    <div class="workflow-text">
                        Handles the visible avatar, objects, materials,
                        textures and 3D rendering.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="workflow-item">

                    <div class="workflow-title">
                        RAM / VRAM
                    </div>

                    <div class="workflow-text">
                        Large models and textures can consume additional
                        memory, especially during importing and preparation.
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    MANY OBJECTS AT ONCE
                </div>

                Launching several objects in a burst is possible, but the
                practical limit depends on the computer being used and on
                how complex those models are.

                Ten simple objects can be very different from ten extremely
                detailed objects with large textures.

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    FIRST LOADS MAY TAKE LONGER
                </div>

                When CIGA prepares an object for the first time, loading can
                take noticeably longer depending on the model.

                Once the relevant resources are prepared and cached,
                repeated use should avoid doing the same preparation again.

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    PRACTICAL GUIDELINE
                </div>

                A large library is not automatically a performance problem.
                The biggest impact usually comes from very complex assets,
                unusually large textures and having many heavy objects active
                and visible at the same time.

                CIGA can prepare resources efficiently, but the final
                performance still depends on the hardware running it.
            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    CIGA DOES ITS BEST
                </div>

                CIGA is designed to handle resources as efficiently as
                reasonably possible, but different computers and 3D models
                will always have different limits.

                The goal is to make the system practical and accessible,
                not to pretend that hardware limitations do not exist.
            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =================================================
         08 TROUBLESHOOTING
    ================================================== -->

    <section class="help-section">

        <div class="section-header">

            <span class="section-number">
                08
            </span>

            <h2 class="section-title">
                TROUBLESHOOTING
            </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="section-content">

            <div class="feature-grid">

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        CIGA TAKES A WHILE TO LOAD
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        This is often caused by a large or complex object
                        being prepared.

                        Check which object CIGA is currently loading and
                        give the application some time to finish if the
                        process is still progressing.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        CIGA SEEMS STUCK
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        If the application stays on the same object for a
                        very long time without progressing, that model may
                        be causing the problem.

                        Try removing that object from the library and start
                        CIGA again.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        AVATAR DOES NOT REACT
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        Check that the correct avatar is loaded and mapped,
                        and make sure the required hit points are available.
                        Then test the interaction manually before checking
                        the event configuration.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="feature">

                    <div class="feature-title">
                        EVENTS DO NOT FIRE
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-text">
                        Check the integration connection first.

                        For StreamElements, confirm that the connection is
                        active. For VMC, confirm that the receiving software
                        is listening on the configured local port.
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="steps">

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        01
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Restart CIGA and reproduce the problem once more.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        02
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Check whether the issue always happens with the same
                        avatar, object, event or integration.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        03
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Check the Godot output for a clear error message.
                        Relevant errors are much more useful than sending
                        the entire output log without context.
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="step">

                    <div class="step-number">
                        04
                    </div>

                    <div class="step-text">
                        Test the simplest possible configuration first:
                        one avatar, one object and one interaction.
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    DEBUGGING INFORMATION
                </div>

                When reporting a problem, include what you were doing when
                it happened, which object or avatar was involved, and any
                relevant error shown by CIGA or Godot.

                This makes it much easier to identify whether the problem is
                related to the model, configuration, integration or runtime.
            </div>

            <div class="note">

                <div class="note-title">
                    OBJECT LOAD PROBLEMS
                </div>

                If CIGA repeatedly becomes stuck while preparing one specific
                object, that object is a useful first suspect.

                Removing the problematic model and restarting the application
                can help confirm whether the asset itself is responsible.
            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


